  "summary": "Three preprints extend Bioconductor containers, network visualization and GO term reduction to handle networks and annotations alongside omics data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is infrastructure for working with biological networks and their annotations. GraphExperiment extends SingleCellExperiment as an R/Bioconductor S4 class that stores feature- and observation-level igraph networks synchronized with omics data, keeping topology and quantitative measurements in one container. NORMA 3.0 is a client-side rewrite for visualizing annotated networks, with group-aware layouts, multi-group node rendering and 21 topological analyses. GOParsimony works on the annotation layer, reducing redundant Gene Ontology term lists by saltating across the GO digraph to find the most parsimonious functional explanations. New elements are network-omics coupling in a standard container, group-aware visualization, and digraph-based term reduction. The summaries as listed report no benchmarks against existing tools.",
